@end menu

@node math-optimisation User Guide
@section User Guide

Users experience this crate as the part of SotF that takes seconds
(speaker EQ) to minutes (multi-position room EQ) and produces filter
sets. The CLI exposes a few user-tweakable knobs:

@itemize @bullet
@item Population size and iteration budget.
@item Strategy: classical DE, current-to-pbest, L-SHADE.
@item Constraint handling: linear, non-linear, or penalty.
@end itemize

@node math-optimisation Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

@subheading DE strategies

@table @code
@item DE/rand/1
@code{x_trial = x_r1 + F * (x_r2 - x_r3)}.
@item DE/best/1
@code{x_trial = x_best + F * (x_r1 - x_r2)}.
@item DE/current-to-best/1
Blend of current and best.
@item DE/rand/2
Five-vector mutation.
@item DE/current-to-pbest/1
SHADE: blend with top-p% individual.
@end table

@subheading L-SHADE

Linear population-size reduction with an external archive of discarded
solutions. @code{F} and @code{CR} adapt via SHADE-style success
histories.

@subheading Other solvers

@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{Levenberg-Marquardt} -- non-linear least squares.
@item @strong{COBYLA} -- non-linear constraints, derivative-free.
@item @strong{ISRES} -- improved stochastic ranking evolution
  strategy.
@end itemize

@subheading Recording evaluations

The solver supports an evaluation recorder that captures every
fitness computation for convergence plotting and regression testing.

@subheading Visualisation

The crate ships a @code{plot-de} binary that renders test functions
and optimisation traces.

@subheading Testing and QA

@example
cargo test -p math-optimisation
just qa
@end example

The QA benchmark suite verifies convergence across the test function
library (@ref{math-test-functions Manual}).
